# React Native horizontal rows

This repo has already hit this bug many times: label + chevron (or value) **stacks vertically** instead of sitting on one row.

## Root causes

1. **`Pressable` + `flexDirection: 'row'`** — On React Native, `Pressable` often does **not** honor row layout on the host. Children stack.
2. **`Text` / `AppText` with `flex: 1`** — Unreliable in a row. Flex belongs on a wrapping `View`.

## Required pattern

Match `SettingsNavRow` (`src/components/ui/SettingsNavRow.jsx`):

```jsx
// ✅ GOOD — row styles on inner View; flex on View, not Text
<Pressable onPress={onPress}>
  {({ pressed }) => (
    <View style={[styles.row, pressed && styles.pressed]}>
      <View style={styles.labelCol}>
        <AppText numberOfLines={1} style={styles.label}>
          {label}
        </AppText>
      </View>
      <View style={styles.chevronCol}>
        <Ionicons name="chevron-forward" size={18} />
      </View>
    </View>
  )}
</Pressable>
```

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — row on Pressable; flex on Text → stacks
<Pressable style={styles.row} onPress={onPress}>
  <AppText style={{ flex: 1 }}>{label}</AppText>
  <Ionicons name="chevron-forward" size={18} />
</Pressable>
```

```js
// styles
row: { flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', width: '100%' },
labelCol: { flex: 1, minWidth: 0, justifyContent: 'center' },
chevronCol: { width: 22, alignItems: 'center', justifyContent: 'center' },
```

## Prefer existing UI

For settings-style rows (label + chevron), use **`SettingsNavRow`** inside **`SettingsSection`** instead of hand-rolling.

## Checklist before shipping a tappable row

- [ ] `flexDirection: 'row'` is on a **`View`**, not on `Pressable`
- [ ] `flex: 1` / `minWidth: 0` is on a **`View`**, not on `AppText`
- [ ] Trailing chevron/value sits in its own fixed-width `View`
